// Dust devils (WorldActorHandler, DustDevilPuff, DustDevilDebris): summoned with /dsactor as the warm-up starts, on a
// flat platform of sand built high over a desert, so no wall or water breaks them up and nothing else is in view. At
// night, so none start on their own: each run has only the summoned ones. A summoned one has a random size and path, so
// compare with --spread. Four, as a few could be in view on a busy afternoon, and twelve, far more than ever start
// naturally. A dust devil lives 37 seconds at least: the warm-up and the recording fit in that. Facing east, downwind
// on the bench world's day (the time is held), so they travel away from the camera and stay in view: facing south they
// drifted out of it to the left, and their drawing went unmeasured. See README.md.
{
  "world": "bench",
  "seed": 20261030,
